> Title: Development 1.0.1
> Note: This is the Development release of 1.0.1, this contains untested features, and stuff that may be removed from the release of 1.0.1.

> What does this release contain:
- Doors
    - Added `Interactive Doors`
        * Look at a door to see its interaction points (Handle, Hinge, Lock, Kick)
        * Reach: 7 studs
        * Actions:
            * Open / Close (Handle)
            * Open slightly (Hinge): opens the door 14° so you can peek through
            * Nudge open / closed: scroll the mouse wheel to move the door 12° at a time
            * Push open: walk into a door that's open slightly (from the side it swings away from) and it swings fully open
            * Kick: breaches the door (1.1 second cooldown between kicks)
            * Lock / Unlock: only from the inside of exterior doors
            * Pick lock: only from the outside of a door you know is locked (see `Lockpicking`)
        * Locked doors:
            * Trying to open a locked door rattles it and tells you it's locked
            * Once you know a door is locked, it only offers `Kick` and `Pick lock`
            * Kicking a locked door has a 40% chance to break it from the push side, and 20% from the pull side
        * Broken doors:
            * Every door you kick open is broken
            * Broken doors can still be closed, but anyone can walk straight through them
            * Broken doors can no longer be locked
        * Door speeds:
            * Normal: 200°/s
            * Slow (peeking / nudging): 90°/s
            * Breach (kicked): 900°/s
        * Wooden and metal doors have their own sounds for opening, closing, creaking, rattling, locking, kicking and breaching
    - Map changes
        * The outside garage door of the Town House is now locked
- Lockpicking
    - Added `Lockpick set`
        * Type: Misc
        * Size: 1x1
        * Stacks: up to 6 (each one is a single pick)
        * Value: 1,200
        * Weight: 0.05 Kg
        * Shows as a zipped leather pouch with the picks sticking out
        * Works from your pockets, rig or backpack
    - Added `Lockpicking Minigame`
        * Use `Pick lock` on a locked door you're outside of
        * The camera moves in close and the background blurs out:
            * You first see the pick slide into the keyhole from the front
            * The lock then swings around to a cut-open side view, showing every pin and spring
        * Controls:
            * [A] / [D]: move the pick between pins
            * [W]: push the pin (it shoots up and springs back down)
            * [Left Mouse Button]: set the pin
            * [F]: abort
        * Setting a pin:
            * Each pin has a green zone at the line where it needs to sit; the zone lights up when it's safe to set
            * Set it while it's in the zone and the pin locks into place, and the pick moves on to the next pin
            * Set every pin to unlock the door
        * Failing:
            * Setting at the wrong time drops that pin back down (the other set pins stay set)
            * Every failed set wears your pick, and after 15 failed sets the pick snaps
            * A snapped pick uses up one lockpick and drops every pin
            * Running out of lockpicks ends the minigame
        * Lock types:
            * Door: 6 pins, brass plate
            * Town House: 5 pins, nickel plate
            * Crate: 4 pins, rusty plate
        * Each lock has random pin heights (5 possible depths), which stay the same until it's picked
        * Pushing, setting, failing and snapping all have their own sounds; nearby players hear the sets, fails and snaps
- Health & Medical
    - Added `Health`
        * Every player and NPC now has 100 Health
        * Deaths now record a cause: Wounds, Bleeding, Organ damage, Blunt force, Explosion, Radiation, Starvation, Void or Admin
    - Added `Body Regions`
        * Each body region now has its own health:
            * Head: 35
            * Thorax: 80
            * Stomach: 70
            * Left Arm / Right Arm: 60
            * Left Leg / Right Leg: 65
        * Each region tracks its own wounds:
            * Light bleeding
            * Heavy bleeding (12 mL/s or more)
            * Fractures
    - Added `Organ Damage`
        * Bullets that reach an organ cause their own bleeding, pain and damage:
            * Brain: always lethal
            * Heart: 140 mL/s bleeding, can cause `Cardiac Arrest`
            * Aorta: 160 mL/s bleeding
            * Lungs: 10 mL/s bleeding, can cause a `Collapsed Lung`
            * Liver: 30 mL/s bleeding
            * Kidneys: 22 mL/s bleeding, very painful
            * Stomach: 6 mL/s bleeding
            * Spine: 4 mL/s bleeding, can cause `Paralysis`
            * Femoral arteries (legs): 50 mL/s bleeding
        * Other conditions: `Leg Fracture`, `Arm Fracture`, `Concussion`
    - Changes to `Blood` & `Pain`
        * Blood volume: 5,000 mL
        * You fall unconscious below 3,000 mL and die below 2,200 mL
        * Too much pain (90 or more) sends you into shock for 5 to 12 seconds
        * Pain fades faster while you're unconscious
        * While unconscious you now see when you'll wake up
    - Changes to `Medical Items`
        * `Army bandage`: stops bleeding below 12 mL/s, halves heavier bleeding and reduces pain
        * `CAT tourniquet`: stops limb bleeding, but causes pain
- Player Interaction
    - Added `Player Menu`
        * Open it on another player or NPC to choose an action
        * Actions:
            * `Health checkup`: shows their pulse, pain, blood level and any conditions (Unconscious, Cardiac Arrest, Collapsed Lung, Concussion, Paralysed, Dead)
            * `Drag` / `Let go`
            * `Invite to squad`
    - Added `Dragging`
        * You can drag players and NPCs that are unconscious or zip-tied
        * Zombies and Traders can't be dragged
        * Reach: 6 studs
        * You walk at 55% speed while dragging
        * The drag breaks if they end up more than 11 studs away
    - Changes to `Zip Ties`
        * Tying someone up takes 2.5 seconds
        * Cutting someone free takes 1.5 seconds
        * Restrained players walk at 60% speed
        * Restrained players can now struggle free: mash [X] 25 times. Progress drains if you slow down
- Weather
    - Added `Rain`
        * The server checks the weather every 90 seconds, with a 40% chance of rain
        * Rain intensity ranges from 25% to 100%, and builds up gradually
        * Wind of up to 14 studs/s pushes the rain sideways
        * Clouds build up with the rain: the sky becomes fully overcast and the clouds thicken and turn grey
    - Added `Storms` & `Lightning`
        * Rain above 65% intensity turns into a storm
        * Lightning strikes every 6 to 26 seconds, between 80 and 1,100 studs away from players
        * Storm clouds turn dark grey, and lightning lights them up
- Footprints
    - Added `Footprints`
        * Walking through mud, dirt, sand, snow, water, blood or other spilled liquids coats your boots
        * Once you step off, your boots leave prints with the tread of your sole
        * Prints get fainter with every step until your boots are clean:
            * Mud: 12 steps
            * Blood: up to 14 steps (fewer if the blood is drying)
            * Other spilled liquids: 8 steps
            * Water: 6 steps
            * Dirt: 5 steps
            * Sand: 4 steps
            * Snow: 3 steps
        * Prints fade away over time:
            * Blood: 160 seconds (darkens from red to dried brown as it fades)
            * Mud: 140 seconds
            * Dirt: 80 seconds
            * Sand: 50 seconds
            * Snow: 30 seconds
            * Water: 25 seconds
        * Your boots dry off 90 seconds after you last stepped in something
        * Prints only form on solid ground (not on vehicles)
        * Everyone can see prints within 140 studs
        * Up to 220 prints at once (fewer on lower graphics settings)
- Visuals & Effects
    - Added `Blood Effects`
        * Gunshot wounds leave blood splatter on nearby surfaces, stretched in the direction of the shot
        * Blood on walls slowly runs downward and drips onto the floor
        * Wounded players drip blood as they move
        * Bodies leave a blood pool that grows over time
        * Blood darkens as it dries (about 2.5 minutes)
        * Up to 160 blood splats at a time; each one fades after 100 seconds
        * Blood is cleaned up once the body it came from is gone
        * Armour that stops a bullet also stops the blood
    - Added `Liquid Simulation`
        * Spilled liquids (water, blood and more) now flow and drip off edges
        * Liquids leave puddles and stains that evaporate over time (water after 90 seconds, blood after 100 seconds)
    - Added `Vehicle Wheel Spray`
        * Vehicles throw up water splashes and mud from their wheels when driving through puddles and mud
        * Visible up to 260 studs away
    - Changes to `Scopes`
        * Scopes now show the eyepiece and a dark vignette when you look through them
        * When scoped, your weapon now has weight: it lags slightly behind where you look (up to 1.5°) and sways 4 times as much
- Audio
    - Added `Acoustics`
        * Gunshots, footsteps, impacts and explosions now echo off the world around you
        * Over 40 materials absorb and reflect sound differently (concrete and metal echo, while fabric, carpet and snow soak it up)
        * Indoors and outdoors now sound different
- Firearms & Ballistics
    - Changes to `Ballistics`
        * Every round now has a real mass and diameter, which affect drop, energy loss and penetration
        * Penetration through walls and other materials has been reworked
    - Changes to `RPG-7`
        * Your camera no longer clips into the launcher when you fire while aiming
    - Changes to `Hit Registration`
        * Shots are now checked against where the target was at the moment you fired, so hits register more reliably for players with higher ping
- Inventory & Economy
    - Changes to `Backpack`
        * Your backpack now counts the same as your pockets and rig
        * You can reload magazines, load loose rounds, and use zip ties, radios and lockpicks straight from your backpack
    - Changes to `Cash`
        * Cash stacks up to 500,000 per stack
        * Earned cash goes into your pockets first, then your backpack
        * Purchases take cash from any of your stacks
    - Changes to `HUD`
        * Food, Water and Stamina bars have been redesigned
        * The weapon slot list now shows empty slots as "Empty"
- Saving
    - Your profile (inventory, appearance and vitals) is now saved when you die, extract, leave, or when the server shuts down
    - If a save fails, the game keeps retrying (every 20 seconds, up to 5 minutes) until it goes through
- General Gameplay Enhancements
    - The game now detects your device (PC, Console or Mobile) and adjusts effects to match:
        * PC: full liquids (260 particles), full blood effects and rain
        * Console: liquids (200 particles), 80% rain
        * Mobile: no liquid simulation, reduced blood effects, 40% rain, and lighter sound processing for better FPS
    - Improved server stability, with limits on how often the server accepts requests from each player
    - Improved server-side protection against exploits
